{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets","id":1455801,"title":"Teleporting unwilling targets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-30T10:44:14-07:00","id":1455801,"title":"Teleporting unwilling targets","content":"Hi. <br /> <br /> What spheres do I need to teleport an unwilling target (human) to a different location?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T11:45:35-07:00","id":1455807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets#post1455801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi.<br /> <br /> What spheres do I need to teleport an unwilling target (human) to a different location?</div> </div> </div> </div>Life and Correspondence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T13:13:03-07:00","id":1455810,"title":"","content":"So I was thinking, but what ranks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","user":"Argonot","date":". 07-30-2021, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T14:28:16-07:00","id":1455814,"title":"","content":"Correspondence three lets you teleport; life to lets you use it to affect living patterns against their will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T14:33:12-07:00","id":1455815,"title":"","content":"Correspondence is 3. Life is a little harder to gage. I could argue that you'd just need 1 to sense the life on a magical level. But I could also see asking for more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24383-laughinggull","name":"LaughingGull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T16:16:37-07:00","id":1455822,"title":"","content":"I feel like 2 dots might be the minimum for Life. Enough to do more than just &quot;sense&quot; it, but not much else. I think they used Matter 2 when discussing Correspondence being used to affect items at a distance, in M20 at least. I think the one exception was if you were reaching through a window made with pure Correspondence and actually using your hand to grab something, etc.? If you want to pull it through the &quot;window,&quot; however, then you need Matter/Life 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T16:49:22-07:00","id":1455826,"title":"","content":"Actually, I wouldn't require life at all, unless you're doing something fancy like teleporting someone's head off of his shoulders. But then, I tend to prefer to minimize the number of spheres needed for any given effect; otherwise, you risk the possibility of a mage who can't do anything useful unless he's got multiple dots in multiple spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T18:36:34-07:00","id":1455829,"title":"","content":"Correspondence 4 and Life 4. Correspondence 4 would be the definite you would need to teleport someone, and Life 4 lets you affect Complex Lifeforms (which humans are). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">otherwise, you risk the possibility of a mage who can't do anything useful unless he's got multiple dots in multiple spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, that's most of Mage without any house rules. I don't forgo the need for multiple Spheres for things (actually, I'm the the opposite, I love making tons of OC Spheres), but I already for a long time removed Paradox completely from my games. That is the thing that really prohibits most stuff from being done, but of course, some may think different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T19:39:37-07:00","id":1455831,"title":"","content":"I imagine many of us house rule one way out another, but the page reference for the rules as written is M20 p.513, last paragraph under correspondence 3. &quot;Also, by combining Correspondence 3 with Forces, Life, or Matter, the mage can move things around from a distance, levitating, manipulating or teleporting them without physical contact.&quot;<br /> <br /> So than the question remains how much life? I'd still go one or two. Three seems excessive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24383-laughinggull","name":"LaughingGull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T20:23:45-07:00","id":1455833,"title":"","content":"Why do you think 2 would be enough to be able to teleport whole human? Something along the lines of 1-3, is only for Simple Lifeforms. Life 4-5 is the definite range per the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T23:47:12-07:00","id":1455837,"title":"","content":"The question you need to ask yourself:<br /> Why would teleporting a huge tree vs. a human require more (or any) knowledge of the Life sphere? Does teleportation of *any* whole(!) pattern require knowledge about the nature of the pattern at all?<br /> <br /> On a note: Yes, I'm with Dataweaver on the 'You don't need extra spheres to teleport a *whole* parttern', as M20 strongly suggests in the pre-levels description paragraph of Correspondence (and then confuses and wrecks with the in-level examples). I don't see why knowledge *about* a pattern would be necessary to just teleport a whole pattern - the nature of the pattern itself should not matter.<br /> <br /> Though, my personal preference aside: Let's presume that, yes, a pattern sphere is necessary, perhaps for locking-on reasons.<br /> The question then becomes, why would teleporting a human require higher knowledge than teleporting a huge tree? If purely for the locking on, Life 2 shouuuld be enough if I recall right.<br /> <br /> An argument *can* be made for a scientific paradigm requiring Life 4, along the lines of Star Trek clone-murd^h^H^H^H^Htransporters, where every bit of a life pattern gets digitized, transported and then re-assembled, maybe. But I am not sure how a more mystic paradigm would require a higher understanding of life for the effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T01:31:24-07:00","id":1455842,"title":"","content":"Because that's what the M20 book on the Life Sphere says. Life 2 only deals with very Simple Lifeforms along the lines of &quot;viruses, mollusks, insects, plants, etc.&quot; For you to teleport a whole person, especially an unwilling one like OP specifies, it would definitely need Life 4 as the M20 information says that. Doesn't matter if its from the Traditions or the Technocracy. Also the point about Correspondence only being able to interact with *Whole Patterns* in the book is to reference that it cannot do things by itself, Correspondence almost always needs other Spheres to work with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T04:15:43-07:00","id":1455845,"title":"","content":"Life 1 detects any Life Pattern, you don't need Life 4 to scan for humans present in a location. Life 2 lets a mage heal themselves, you don't need Life 4 to self-heal just because as a mage you'd be a human. Etc.<br /> <br /> While Life certainly provides a scale of complexity of life that you can use Life on in a broad sense, that scale doesn't determine everything you can do with the Sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T05:43:42-07:00","id":1455848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1455842#post1455842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that's what the M20 book on the Life Sphere says. Life 2 only deals with very Simple Lifeforms along the lines of &quot;viruses, mollusks, insects, plants, etc.&quot; For you to teleport a whole person, especially an unwilling one like OP specifies, it would definitely need Life 4 as the M20 information says that. Doesn't matter if its from the Traditions or the Technocracy. Also the point about Correspondence only being able to interact with *Whole Patterns* in the book is to reference that it cannot do things by itself, Correspondence almost always needs other Spheres to work with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But you can actually damage people with Life 3 already. What would you need Life 4 to &quot;lock an effect on a human&quot; when you can literally liquify his/her organs with Life 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T07:38:11-07:00","id":1455851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1455845#post1455845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life 1 detects any Life Pattern, you don't need Life 4 to scan for humans present in a location. Life 2 lets a mage heal themselves, you don't need Life 4 to self-heal just because as a mage you'd be a human. Etc.<br /> <br /> While Life certainly provides a scale of complexity of life that you can use Life on in a broad sense, that scale doesn't determine everything you can do with the Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but OP was asking about teleporting people, not about healing or self-healing at all. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you can actually damage people with Life 3 already. What would you need Life 4 to &quot;lock an effect on a human&quot; when you can literally liquify his/her organs with Life 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess an adjusted definite range to begin teleporting people, would be 3-5, since the Life 3 section blurb says you can now finally begin to &quot;Heal or Harm&quot; complex organisms at that point. Though Life 4 is when it specifically begins to outright mention people, especially since you want to teleport an unwilling target to yourself or another location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T08:18:28-07:00","id":1455853,"title":"","content":"I'd say willing and unwilling target doesn't matter to the spheres needed. Might matter to the difficulty, if the unwilling target is moving around lots. The main rational for this is few other spheres depend on the targets willingness to have the magic effect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T08:48:44-07:00","id":1455854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1455837#post1455837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question you need to ask yourself:<br /> Why would teleporting a huge tree vs. a human require more (or any) knowledge of the Life sphere? Does teleportation of *any* whole(!) pattern require knowledge about the nature of the pattern at all?<br /> <br /> On a note: Yes, I'm with Dataweaver on the 'You don't need extra spheres to teleport a *whole* parttern', as M20 strongly suggests in the pre-levels description paragraph of Correspondence (and then confuses and wrecks with the in-level examples). I don't see why knowledge *about* a pattern would be necessary to just teleport a whole pattern - the nature of the pattern itself should not matter.<br /> <br /> Though, my personal preference aside: Let's presume that, yes, a pattern sphere is necessary, perhaps for locking-on reasons.<br /> The question then becomes, why would teleporting a human require higher knowledge than teleporting a huge tree? If purely for the locking on, Life 2 shouuuld be enough if I recall right.<br /> <br /> An argument *can* be made for a scientific paradigm requiring Life 4, along the lines of Star Trek clone-murd^h^H^H^H^Htransporters, where every bit of a life pattern gets digitized, transported and then re-assembled, maybe. But I am not sure how a more mystic paradigm would require a higher understanding of life for the effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going back, you're totally right; the introduction section to Correspondence in M20 uses Dataweaver's example of decapitating someone (altering the Pattern) versus snatching a gun away from someone (moving a whole Pattern), while the dot descriptions regularly reference needing other Spheres, though they're much more ambiguous. It seems like a case where contradictory material from different editions was thrown in, and missed in the editing.<br /> <br /> Regarding dots of Life and how complex the life-forms are, I'm pretty sure that's specifically in reference to making alterations and transmutations. As others have noted, there are examples given of Effects being used on more complex life-forms at lower levels, while the discussion of how simple or complex a life-form is almost always seems to be discussed in the context of transmutation. Maybe you'd need Life 3 instead of 2 to remove a small internal organ instead of an entire head, Life 4 or 5 to remove cancer from someone (assuming you had some weird reason to teleport the cancer out of someone's body instead of just curing it with pure Life).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T14:01:15-07:00","id":1455874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1455851#post1455851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but OP was asking about teleporting people, not about healing or self-healing at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which applies just as much to your claim that locking on to Life patterns should be an exception to the lock-on rules. My point is simply that there's more to Life than what you're making it sound like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1455853#post1455853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say willing and unwilling target doesn't matter to the spheres needed. Might matter to the difficulty, if the unwilling target is moving around lots. The main rational for this is few other spheres depend on the targets willingness to have the magic effect them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that difficulty isn't really something that can change in all this. There isn't a difficulty modifier for unwilling targets, nor a requirement for more successes.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that there's a game-play element here, as &quot;teleport them into [insta-death of whatever source]&quot; is rather simple if it just takes Corr 3. It doesn't take some sort of exciting creativity, or lots of arduous prep work. It's easily the scene from Thor:Ragnarok where Dr. Strange sends Loki falling for half an hour with a simple gesture... but easily lethal and capable of TPKs. Forcible teleportation has been something the system wants to make either resistible, or more difficult than it might be strictly by metaphysics; the problem is the game doesn't give itself a lot of tools to do this. Basically it's either making it higher Corr, or making it take more Spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T15:23:53-07:00","id":1455878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1455874#post1455874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that difficulty isn't really something that can change in all this. There isn't a difficulty modifier for unwilling targets, nor a requirement for more successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was meaning that picking up a target that is moving around lot may be more difficult than a target who is still.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1455874#post1455874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that there's a game-play element here, as &quot;teleport them into [insta-death of whatever source]&quot; is rather simple if it just takes Corr 3. It doesn't take some sort of exciting creativity, or lots of arduous prep work. It's easily the scene from Thor:Ragnarok where Dr. Strange sends Loki falling for half an hour with a simple gesture... but easily lethal and capable of TPKs. Forcible teleportation has been something the system wants to make either resistible, or more difficult than it might be strictly by metaphysics; the problem is the game doesn't give itself a lot of tools to do this. Basically it's either making it higher Corr, or making it take more Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>But to do this well means knowing the nature of the insta-death in advance, where it is, and how far and so forth. Yes for the teleportation of living things Life is needed, I'd see at 2 personally, alongside Correspondence 3 or 4 depending on how it is been done. Though the Tether rules [<i>How do you do that</i> p78] suggest Life 4.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd agree in part about the not wanting insta-death, but if someone has put in the work to get insta-death option and can deploy it, why stop it. I personally don't see a reason why the game should not have it. However would agree that needing the Sphere of life alongside that Cor is true. However applying this logic then some one with Life 4 or 5 also has insta-death options, as does Entropy at the same level, and possibly Force, and if used in creative ways Matter and Time, many of these are no resistable as well. The main game based restriction on these I'd see is paradgim and focus.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T17:38:18-07:00","id":1455889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1455878#post1455878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was meaning that picking up a target that is moving around lot may be more difficult than a target who is still.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only place to put this is for an aimed spell... which most people ignore over locking on because then you don't have to worry about precisely this. An aimed spell can be dodged/etc. and is subject to anything that might interfere with a ranged attack (the roll itself has a chance of failing to account for a moving target even if they're unaware to defend themselves). Dealing with multiple targets also gets more complicated than increasing the successes needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But to do this well means knowing the nature of the insta-death in advance, where it is, and how far and so forth. </div> </div> </div>12 miles straight up (this is an approximation of the Armstrong limit; aka how high up in our atmosphere you can go without mechanical aid and survive without immediate medical attention), which isn't terribly far by Correspondence standards, and relies on nature doing all the hard work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd agree in part about the not wanting insta-death, but if someone has put in the work to get insta-death option and can deploy it, why stop it. </div> </div> </div>That's the problem with starting level characters being able to access pretty reliable insta-death powers: it doesn't get to the &quot;put in the work,&quot; part of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However applying this logic then some one with Life 4 or 5 also has insta-death options, as does Entropy at the same level, and possibly Force, and if used in creative ways Matter and Time, many of these are no resistable as well. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what specifically you're referring to, but almost all of these are either bound by the damage rules (Entropy 4 does damage like any other magical attack, rather than allowing insta-death just by hitting someone with it), or create dangerous situations that could kill people but people can also try to get away from them (and also have other complications like putting the casting mage at risk).<br /> <br /> The higher the level, the higher the magical difficulty (including the higher cap on how low you can get the difficulty with various bonuses), and thus even harder to cope with many of these things being vulgar. Many of these sorts of effects are more scary because of the area of effect rather than the ability to smite one individual enemy. Forces 5 is scary because you can set a city on fire, not because it's actually that much better at killing one person than Forces 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main game based restriction on these I'd see is paradgim and focus.<br /> </div> </div> </div>These are rarely effective restrictions on things like &quot;can I forcibly teleport someone,&quot; once teleporting people is already a thing you can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T17:53:44-07:00","id":1455891,"title":"","content":"The main restriction that I would put on it would be to require additional successes if the target is unwilling. But really, that's more a matter of counter magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T20:37:46-07:00","id":1455895,"title":"","content":"If I'm not mistaken, teleporting someone else already requires at least 3 successes because you're affecting someone other than yourself in a significantly magical fashion. Doesn't it? Typical OP teleporting someone to instant death like, say, &quot;the sun&quot; or &quot;inside an active volcano&quot; would likely require more because of the Correspondence Table (getting &quot;sympathy&quot; with such an &quot;instant death&quot; place takes some effort, rewarded with easy teleports).<br /> <br /> The 6 or so successes that these things tend to require it's more than enough to instantly kill anyone that hasn't special supernatural protections. In Mage, that Technocrat you're trying to send to kiss the sun it's potentially going to have some way to resist this (say, Primium). Having that in count, is it trully that gamebreaking?.<br /> <br /> We're talking on getting the successes needed to teleport + some to bypass the potential resistance here. This is an all or nothing affair, you're not going to get the reward of causing &quot;some&quot; damage if it doesn't get enough successes for the instant kill. It's also Vulgar.<br /> <br /> I see it would be the better option against some form of enemies (A Life-made abomination with loads of hp, regen, and soack?), but I don't see it becoming the dominant strategy until you get into crossover (as many builds from other splats are capable of soacking obscene amounts of damage, but don't have anything specific against this type of &quot;reality warping&quot;). I think this is the reason M20 gives all supers Countermagick. I don't love that rule, and I'm not sure it trully solves the core issues, but I think that's the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-31-2021, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T21:14:59-07:00","id":1455897,"title":"","content":"+1 for understanding the reason for Night-Folk Countermagic in M20 while also utterly hating the current rules and trying to figure out better house-rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T14:45:13-07:00","id":1455956,"title":"","content":"If you're getting enough successes to teleport a Vampire to the sun (or a sunny place), you could have gotten enough successes to kill them with aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Mages who click their fingers and send someone to the sun ARE OP, but Mage PCs don't act that way unless they hit a very high Arete, get a specialization in Teleporting, get a lucky roll...<br /> <br /> With 6 successes you *could* have just melted them with a Forces attack, and gotten more successes thanks to a lower difficulty. It's also harder to make teleporting someone coincidental compared to exploding a boiler or making a fire blow in their direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T14:03:07-07:00","id":1456089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1455829#post1455829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correspondence 4 and Life 4. Correspondence 4 would be the definite you would need to teleport someone, and Life 4 lets you affect Complex Lifeforms (which humans are). <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Lol, that's most of Mage without any house rules. I don't forgo the need for multiple Spheres for things (actually, I'm the the opposite, I love making tons of OC Spheres), but I already for a long time removed Paradox completely from my games. That is the thing that really prohibits most stuff from being done, but of course, some may think different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, not if you do the sane thing and ignore HDYDT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T18:10:00-07:00","id":1456271,"title":"","content":"On the question of insta-death: You can kill a target with Life alone. If a Mage is going to the trouble of using Correspondence and Life to teleport an unwilling target, Capturing the target alive would more often be the intent (even if the caster in this instance is doing it to put someone into a volcano just for style). It could also be used to test a disciple by sending them on a difficult journey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T05:00:09-07:00","id":1456295,"title":"","content":"There is no &quot;insta-death&quot; Life power. There's just rolling enough successes to do enough damage to kill them (and possible overcome soak if the target can).<br /> <br /> Teleporting the unwilling requires a subjective number of successes (despite my example of a much more reasonable insta-death option on teleportation, people continually focus on things like all the way to the sun... even if though most people see the sun everyday and are quite familiar with it even if it's very far away because it's not about actual distance), and can be done to insta-kill people, hence the game requiring more out of teleporting people than might seem necessary","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T09:03:06-07:00","id":1456303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1456295#post1456295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no &quot;insta-death&quot; Life power. There's just rolling enough successes to do enough damage to kill them (and possible overcome soak if the target can).</div> </div> </div> </div>Using Life 4 or 5, alter the body to of a human to breath water rather than air, that's close to insta-death, or alter to composition of blood to be corrosive. All within the perview of Life powers. Then there would be the sealing up of mouth and nose with skin so the target can no longer breath. The effect doesn't directly kill them, it's the knock of the effect that does.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T13:52:02-07:00","id":1456312,"title":"","content":"So, something that requires at least two Life 4 effects, with a base success feat of 4 successes as altering someone else's form is actually a listed example (or if you use HDYDT it could just be one effect that takes 8+ successes so.... not exactly &quot;instant&quot; when you're forced to ritual cast it); giving someone gills and taking away their lungs are two different things. And then fleshcrafting which isn't specifically listed as a Life effect, and seems more a Life/Matter combo at a minimum (molding flesh like clay is an understood simile for a reason...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T16:23:20-07:00","id":1456318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1456271#post1456271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the question of insta-death: You can kill a target with Life alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>... by scoring enough successes. The person dies right away, even if it doesn't qualify as insta-death. My point was about other uses than killing.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1456295#post1456295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teleporting the unwilling requires a subjective number of successes (despite my example of a much more reasonable insta-death option on teleportation, people continually focus on things like all the way to the sun... even if though most people see the sun everyday and are quite familiar with it even if it's very far away because it's not about actual distance), and can be done to insta-kill people, hence the game requiring more out of teleporting people than might seem necessary</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be easier, teleporting someone into the municipal incinerator while nobody there is looking or teleporting them to the sun?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1456303#post1456303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Using Life 4 or 5, alter the body to of a human to breath water rather than air, that's close to insta-death, or alter to composition of blood to be corrosive. All within the perview of Life powers. Then there would be the sealing up of mouth and nose with skin so the target can no longer breath. The effect doesn't directly kill them, it's the knock of the effect that does.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Target the spinal cord in the back of the neck and sever the link with the body (without obviously decapitating the target).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T16:54:17-07:00","id":1456319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1456318#post1456318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would be easier, teleporting someone into the municipal incinerator while nobody there is looking or teleporting them to the sun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on whether you use Correspondence, Void Correspondence, or Data, and how familiar you are with the municipal incinerator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T17:27:47-07:00","id":1456323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1456319#post1456319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on whether you use Correspondence, Void Correspondence, or Data, and how familiar you are with the municipal incinerator.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is Void Correspondence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T19:01:57-07:00","id":1456326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1456323#post1456323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> What is Void Correspondence?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Void Engineer version of Correspondence which takes distance into account rather than sympathetic connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T19:18:17-07:00","id":1456327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1456318#post1456318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... by scoring enough successes. The person dies right away, even if it doesn't qualify as insta-death. My point was about other uses than killing.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that definition a mundane punch is an insta-death effect because you can roll enough successes to kill someone with a punch.<br /> <br /> If the point is about other uses, all of the, &quot;Life can insta kill too with Life 5, Arete 10, and tossing around huge numbers of successes,&quot; doesn't really seem to be on point.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which would be easier, teleporting someone into the municipal incinerator while nobody there is looking or teleporting them to the sun? </div> </div> </div>With standard Correspondence? How well do you know the incinerator/is it in your immediate perceptions? If you can sense the municipal incinerator facility, it's 1 success, if you worked there for years, its 2 successes, if you've read about it online it's 5 successes. You see the sun all the time, even if you probably have never been there, so it's probably 2 or 3 successes depending on your ST's call.<br /> <br /> That's sort of the whole thing. Correspondence doesn't care about the actual distance, it cares about experiential connections.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Target the spinal cord in the back of the neck and sever the link with the body (without obviously decapitating the target). </div> </div> </div>It's still handled as damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T21:24:17-07:00","id":1456332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1456327#post1456327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With standard Correspondence? How well do you know the incinerator/is it in your immediate perceptions? If you can sense the municipal incinerator facility, it's 1 success, if you worked there for years, its 2 successes, if you've read about it online it's 5 successes. You see the sun all the time, even if you probably have never been there, so it's probably 2 or 3 successes depending on your ST's call.<br /> <br /> That's sort of the whole thing. Correspondence doesn't care about the actual distance, it cares about experiential connections.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case where you are capturing someone, the location could be your own basement, a cave, a sealed mining tunnel or a small island in the Pacific. These can be visited without having to pretend to be a city worker or be vaporized by roiling hydrogen.<br /> <br /> Effects that keep important characters in the story are much needed in a world with high powered guns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T11:40:47-07:00","id":1456358,"title":"","content":"But... that's the problem. Teleporting unwilling targets is equally difficult if you're trying to lock them up, or trying to put them in a place that's insta-death. To me, it's actually harder to not kill them (unlike all the talk of Life effects) because getting a low Correspondence target to a secure location requires a lot more prep than looking up in the sky, seeing the Armstrong limit (that perception of there being a &quot;dome&quot; of the sky during the day is where that is, even though the limit isn't responsible for that optical effect). and then only needing 1 success to send someone as high up as you can see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T13:21:31-07:00","id":1456368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1456358#post1456358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, it's actually harder to not kill them (unlike all the talk of Life effects) because getting a low Correspondence target to a secure location requires a lot more prep than looking up in the sky,</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't refer to this option in my example because, even though all versions are vulgar and possibly with some Sleeper witnesses, you stand to create a lot more witnesses by having the target fall from the sky. Most Mages would be trying to minimize the amount of attention drawn to themselves. The sky above is certainly an easy target. So is my basement or a place that I have spent time preparing to hold someone. I am familiar with these places. <br /> <br /> Dropping a pursuing Black Suit onto the parking lot of a Construct would be an effective way of warning your adversary not to waste any more agents.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T13:48:08-07:00","id":1456370,"title":"","content":"Witnesses that see the body after the fact don't count towards the magical difficulty, and are highly unlikely to be able to connect it back to you (a body falling from 12 miles up is not going to fall straight down, that's 12 miles of wind currents blowing them around every which way).<br /> <br /> Teleporting an enemy into your basement because it's easy isn't a great idea if it isn't prepared. If it is a prepared space, well there's all the work that went into that, and the potential witnesses/paper trail of constructing a prison in your home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T18:14:37-07:00","id":1456382,"title":"","content":"The number of witnesses doesn't matter: one or a thousand of them, the worst they can do is to make an Effect Vulgar with Witnesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T20:17:45-07:00","id":1456386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1455801-teleporting-unwilling-targets?p=1456382#post1456382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The number of witnesses doesn't matter: one or a thousand of them, the worst they can do is to make an Effect Vulgar with Witnesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of that. I was saying the Mage would avoid to many witnesses to avoid attention, not Paradox.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T21:05:19-07:00","id":1456390,"title":"","content":"I would require something like Correspondence 4 (teleporting someone other than yourself,) and Life 1 to designate the pattern to be teleported. I'm sensitive to arguments about needing higher levels of Life to affect increasingly complex life forms, however, it seems to me that there's a difference between manipulating the actual life pattern itself and simply designating it for teleportation. The distinction for me is that manipulating or altering the actual pattern requires a certain degree of understanding of what the pattern is, how it works, etc. It doesn't make sense to me that you'd need an intimate or in-depth understanding of the inner workings, or essential nature of that pattern, if the mage is &quot;simply&quot; changing its location via Correspondence. I also tend to use the number of successes required as the main barrier to actually pulling this off.<br /> <br /> Whether this makes &quot;insta-killing&quot; other characters too easy (or whether any other construction makes it too difficult,) seems almost like a matter of taste. Despite the fact that I'm personally persuaded of what I described above being the most reasonable way to interpret the metaphysics and rules of the games, I wouldn't defend that construction as actually being the most reasonable (because what standard would even use to judge that kind of discussion or argument); in fact, I could probably construct a textual justification for practically any interpretation by working backwards from the desired conclusion. It's a pretty loosey goosey game (and it's a good thing too!)<br /> <br /> Edited: To change first mention of Life to Life 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 08-10-2021, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}